  "content": {
    "id": "p10-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p10-q7-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Expand $(1+\\sqrt2)^2$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3+2\\sqrt2$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(1+\\sqrt2)^2&=1^2+2(1)(\\sqrt2)+(\\sqrt2)^2\\\\(1+\\sqrt2)^2&=1+2\\sqrt2+2\\\\(1+\\sqrt2)^2&=3+2\\sqrt2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q7-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence, simplify $\\sqrt{3+2\\sqrt2}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1+\\sqrt2$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\sqrt{3+2\\sqrt2}&=\\sqrt{(1+\\sqrt2)^2}\\\\\\sqrt{3+2\\sqrt2}&=1+\\sqrt2\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe positive square root is used since $1+\\sqrt2>0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q7-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Expand $(\\sqrt a+\\sqrt b)^2$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a+b+2\\sqrt{ab}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(\\sqrt a+\\sqrt b)^2&=(\\sqrt a)^2+2\\sqrt a\\sqrt b+(\\sqrt b)^2\\\\(\\sqrt a+\\sqrt b)^2&=a+b+2\\sqrt{ab}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q7-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Use the previous result to show that $\\sqrt{5+2\\sqrt6}=\\sqrt2+\\sqrt3$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\sqrt{5+2\\sqrt6}=\\sqrt2+\\sqrt3$.\n\nSet $a=2$ and $b=3$ in part (c), then take the positive square root.",
          "worked": "Set $a=2$ and $b=3$ in part (c).\n\n$$\\begin{align*}(\\sqrt2+\\sqrt3)^2&=2+3+2\\sqrt{2\\times3}\\\\(\\sqrt2+\\sqrt3)^2&=5+2\\sqrt6\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $\\sqrt2+\\sqrt3>0$, taking the positive square root gives $\\sqrt{5+2\\sqrt6}=\\sqrt2+\\sqrt3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q7-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "Find positive integers $m$ and $n$ if $\\sqrt{7+2\\sqrt{10}}=\\sqrt m+\\sqrt n$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$m=2,\\ n=5$, or $m=5,\\ n=2$.\n\nChoose radicands with sum $7$ and product $10$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(\\sqrt m+\\sqrt n)^2&=m+n+2\\sqrt{mn}\\\\(\\sqrt2+\\sqrt5)^2&=2+5+2\\sqrt{2\\times5}\\\\(\\sqrt2+\\sqrt5)^2&=7+2\\sqrt{10}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThus $m=2,\\ n=5$, or the reverse order. As both roots are positive, $\\sqrt{7+2\\sqrt{10}}=\\sqrt2+\\sqrt5$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      }
    ]
  },
